Modified by ogadra: mark each sidebar tab and space whose panes run no agent with a square icon for its shells' command state, read from whether a shell's foreground process group is its own: running while a command holds the terminal, unread once one finishes while no client views the tab until a client does, and idle otherwise, colored like the agent states they mirror; a space takes the state of the tab that most needs attention. Applied to herdr v0.9.5 (Apache-2.0).

